   "source": [
    "# Classification d'images Chats vs Chiens — CNN & augmentation de données\n",
    "\n",
    "Projet complet de **classification binaire** (chats vs chiens) avec un réseau de neurones\n",
    "convolutif (CNN) en Keras/TensorFlow. On couvre le pipeline d'entrée, l'augmentation de données,\n",
    "l'entraînement (avec/sans augmentation), l'évaluation (matrice de confusion, précision/rappel),\n",
    "l'inférence sur un jeu de test non étiqueté, la gestion du déséquilibre de classes, la\n",
    "sauvegarde des artefacts et des extensions (transfer learning).\n",
    "\n",
    "> ⚠️ **À exécuter sur une machine avec GPU** (ex. VM DigitalOcean / Colab GPU). L'entraînement\n",
    "> d'un CNN sur des milliers d'images est lent sur CPU.\n",
    ">\n",
    "> **Données :** téléchargez le dataset Cats vs Dogs, dézippez-le, **renommez** le dossier en\n",
    "> `cats_dogs` et placez-le dans un dossier `data/` à côté de ce notebook. Structure attendue :\n",
    "> `data/cats_dogs/train/train/...` et `data/cats_dogs/test/test/...`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5f8d25a8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 0. Réduction de résolution (variables globales)\n",
    "\n",
    "Le dataset est en haute résolution. On réduit à **48×48** via `IMG_HEIGHT`/`IMG_WIDTH` pour\n",
    "alléger le calcul (modifiable)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "45d4cd35",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Chargement des données et générateurs\n",
    "\n",
    "**Bloc prérempli — à copier/exécuter tel quel.** Il construit trois générateurs :\n",
    "`train_flow` (avec augmentation), `val_flow` (redimensionnement seul), `test_flow` (non étiqueté)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "087fb1ca",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Prefilled. Just copy and execute.\n",
    "import os, math, re, random\n",
    "from glob import glob\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import tensorflow as tf\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras.preprocessing.image import ImageDataGenerator\n",
    "\n",
    "np.random.seed(42); tf.random.set_seed(42)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Paths - change if needed\n",
    "DATA_ROOT = Path(\"data/cats_dogs\")\n",
    "train_dir = (DATA_ROOT / \"train\" / \"train\") if (DATA_ROOT / \"train\" / \"train\").exists() else (DATA_ROOT / \"train\")\n",
    "test_dir  = (DATA_ROOT / \"test\"  / \"test\")  if (DATA_ROOT / \"test\"  / \"test\").exists()  else (DATA_ROOT / \"test\")\n",
    "\n",
    "IMG_HEIGHT, IMG_WIDTH = 48, 48   # réduction de résolution\n",
    "batch_size = 32\n",
    "seed = 1337\n",
    "\n",
    "# Build DataFrames from folders\n",
    "def build_df_from_folder(folder: Path, labeled: bool=True):\n",
    "    exts = ('*.jpg','*.jpeg','*.png','*.bmp')\n",
    "    files = []\n",
    "    for ex in exts:\n",
    "        files.extend(glob(str(folder / '**' / ex), recursive=True))\n",
    "    if not files:\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"No images found under {folder}\")\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    for f in files:\n",
    "        if labeled:\n",
    "            name = Path(f).name.lower()\n",
    "            parent = Path(f).parent.name.lower()\n",
    "            if parent in {\"cat\",\"cats\"}:\n",
    "                label = \"cat\"\n",
    "            elif parent in {\"dog\",\"dogs\"}:\n",
    "                label = \"dog\"\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                if re.search(r'(^|[^a-z])cat([^a-z]|$)', name): label = \"cat\"\n",
    "                elif re.search(r'(^|[^a-z])dog([^a-z]|$)', name): label = \"dog\"\n",
    "                else:\n",
    "                    continue\n",
    "            rows.append({\"filepath\": f, \"label\": label})\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            rows.append({\"filepath\": f})\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "\n",
    "df_train_full = build_df_from_folder(train_dir, labeled=True)\n",
    "df_test_full  = build_df_from_folder(test_dir,  labeled=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Train validation split\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "df_tr, df_val = train_test_split(\n",
    "    df_train_full, test_size=0.2, stratify=df_train_full[\"label\"], random_state=seed\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generators\n",
    "train_gen = ImageDataGenerator(\n",
    "    rescale=1./255,\n",
    "    rotation_range=45,\n",
    "    width_shift_range=0.15,\n",
    "    height_shift_range=0.15,\n",
    "    zoom_range=0.5,\n",
    "    horizontal_flip=True,\n",
    ")\n",
    "val_gen = ImageDataGenerator(rescale=1./255)\n",
    "test_gen = ImageDataGenerator(rescale=1./255)\n",
    "\n",
    "train_flow = train_gen.flow_from_dataframe(\n",
    "    df_tr, x_col=\"filepath\", y_col=\"label\",\n",
    "    target_size=(IMG_HEIGHT, IMG_WIDTH),\n",
    "    class_mode=\"binary\", batch_size=batch_size,\n",
    "    shuffle=True, seed=seed, validate_filenames=False\n",
    ")\n",
    "val_flow = val_gen.flow_from_dataframe(\n",
    "    df_val, x_col=\"filepath\", y_col=\"label\",\n",
    "    target_size=(IMG_HEIGHT, IMG_WIDTH),\n",
    "    class_mode=\"binary\", batch_size=batch_size,\n",
    "    shuffle=False, validate_filenames=False\n",
    ")\n",
    "# Unlabeled test for inference only\n",
    "test_flow = test_gen.flow_from_dataframe(\n",
    "    df_test_full, x_col=\"filepath\", y_col=None,\n",
    "    target_size=(IMG_HEIGHT, IMG_WIDTH),\n",
    "    class_mode=None, batch_size=batch_size,\n",
    "    shuffle=False, validate_filenames=False\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print({\"train\": train_flow.samples, \"val\": val_flow.samples, \"test\": test_flow.samples,\n",
    "       \"class_indices\": train_flow.class_indices})"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "73b69dfc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Examiner les données\n",
    "\n",
    "**À faire** — équilibre des classes, grille d'exemples, indices visuels."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "dfff9ee7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Nombre d'images d'entraînement par classe\n",
    "import collections\n",
    "idx_to_class = {v: k for k, v in train_flow.class_indices.items()}\n",
    "counts = collections.Counter(train_flow.labels)\n",
    "class_counts = {idx_to_class[i]: n for i, n in counts.items()}\n",
    "print(\"Images d'entraînement par classe :\", class_counts)\n",
    "\n",
    "total = sum(class_counts.values())\n",
    "for cls, n in class_counts.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"  {cls}: {n} ({100*n/total:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ratio = max(class_counts.values()) / min(class_counts.values())\n",
    "print(f\"\\nRatio majorité/minorité : {ratio:.2f}  ->\",\n",
    "      \"équilibré\" if ratio < 1.2 else \"déséquilibré\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0333717f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Grille d'exemples annotés\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "images, labels = next(train_flow)\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 8))\n",
    "for i in range(min(9, len(images))):\n",
    "    plt.subplot(3, 3, i + 1)\n",
