   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Comparaison base (sans augmentation) vs augmentation\n",
    "\n",
    "On entraîne un modèle **identique** mais sur des données **sans augmentation**, et on compare."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e495c7d7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Générateur d'entraînement SANS augmentation (redimensionnement + rescale uniquement)\n",
    "noaug_gen = ImageDataGenerator(rescale=1./255)\n",
    "noaug_flow = noaug_gen.flow_from_dataframe(\n",
    "    df_tr, x_col=\"filepath\", y_col=\"label\",\n",
    "    target_size=(IMG_HEIGHT, IMG_WIDTH),\n",
    "    class_mode=\"binary\", batch_size=batch_size,\n",
    "    shuffle=True, seed=seed, validate_filenames=False\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "baseline = build_cnn()\n",
    "baseline.compile(optimizer=tf.keras.optimizers.Adam(1e-3),\n",
    "                 loss=\"binary_crossentropy\", metrics=[\"accuracy\"])\n",
    "baseline_history = baseline.fit(\n",
    "    noaug_flow, validation_data=val_flow, epochs=EPOCHS,\n",
    "    callbacks=[tf.keras.callbacks.EarlyStopping(monitor=\"val_loss\", patience=5,\n",
    "                                                restore_best_weights=True)],\n",
    "    verbose=1,\n",
    ")\n",
    "plot_history(baseline_history, \"(base, sans augmentation)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b898018d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Comparaison des métriques de validation\n",
    "base_loss, base_acc = baseline.evaluate(val_flow, verbose=0)\n",
    "aug_loss, aug_acc = model.evaluate(val_flow, verbose=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "compare_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"modèle\": [\"base (sans aug)\", \"augmenté\"],\n",
    "    \"val_loss\": [base_loss, aug_loss],\n",
    "    \"val_accuracy\": [base_acc, aug_acc],\n",
    "})\n",
    "display(compare_df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e392ddc0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Analyse de l'écart de généralisation :** le modèle de base a tendance à mieux coller aux\n",
    "données d'entraînement (perte train plus basse) mais à généraliser moins bien (val_loss plus\n",
    "haute, courbes qui divergent tôt) → surapprentissage. Le modèle **augmenté** montre un écart\n",
    "train/val plus faible et une meilleure `val_accuracy` : l'augmentation agit comme régularisation\n",
    "sans ajouter de paramètres."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "be6527cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Gestion du déséquilibre de classes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a6901388",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.utils.class_weight import compute_class_weight\n",
    "\n",
    "y_int = np.array(train_flow.labels)\n",
    "weights = compute_class_weight(\"balanced\", classes=np.unique(y_int), y=y_int)\n",
    "class_weight = {int(c): float(w) for c, w in zip(np.unique(y_int), weights)}\n",
    "print(\"Poids de classes :\", class_weight)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Réentraînement avec class_weight (utile surtout si déséquilibre marqué)\n",
    "model_cw = build_cnn()\n",
    "model_cw.compile(optimizer=tf.keras.optimizers.Adam(1e-3),\n",
    "                 loss=\"binary_crossentropy\", metrics=[\"accuracy\"])\n",
    "history_cw = model_cw.fit(\n",
    "    train_flow, validation_data=val_flow, epochs=EPOCHS,\n",
    "    class_weight=class_weight, callbacks=callbacks, verbose=1,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "val_flow.reset()\n",
    "cw_preds = (model_cw.predict(val_flow, verbose=0).ravel() >= 0.5).astype(int)\n",
    "print(classification_report(val_flow.labels, cw_preds,\n",
    "                            target_names=[idx_to_class[0], idx_to_class[1]]))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "577de6c6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Effet attendu :** en pénalisant davantage les erreurs sur la classe minoritaire,\n",
    "`class_weight` **augmente son rappel** (moins de faux négatifs), parfois au prix d'une légère\n",
    "baisse de précision. Si les classes sont déjà équilibrées, l'effet est négligeable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "073d9e71",
